; worldwear.eval - the doll's wear slots follow the world in hand (code-review
; C330). Judged by tools/WorldTest.py phase 51. The UI keeps its own copy of
; each item's catalog fields (category, weight, holdable, `wear`), rebuilt when
; a world loads - and the wear slots were the one map that rebuild never
; cleared, so after a switch to a world where an item had lost its `wear` the
; doll still took it in the slot the last world gave it.
;
; `wear` puts an item on the doll by the doll's own rule (the UI's bank), so it
; is the doll asked from a script. WorldTest makes wt_wear, a copy of its scratch
; world whose padded_jack has no `wear`, and runs this with the scratch world
; open (`dungeon-demo` below is replaced by its name).
;
;   --- here ---    the jack is worn, on the body (THE CONTROL: it can be).
;   --- there ---   after the switch to wt_wear, wearing it is REFUSED.
;   --- back ---    and back in the first world it is worn again.
logecho on
reset
echo --- here ---
wear padded_jack 0
wear none 0
worlds load wt_wear
reset
echo --- there ---
expect-refuse wear padded_jack 0
worlds load dungeon-demo
reset
echo --- back ---
wear padded_jack 0
echo --- end ---
